{"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "Please run an indirect anti-Salmonella IgY ELISA on our submitted egg yolk samples using the following protocol:\n\n1. Coat clear, U-bottom 96-well plates (Thermo Fisher #268200) with 2 \u00b5g/well of Salmonella Typhimurium LPS (Sigma #L3129) prepared in 1X ELISA Coating Buffer (BioLegend #421701). Incubate overnight at 4\u00b0C.\n2. Wash the wells 4 times with PBS-Tween-20.\n3. Block the wells with 3% non-fat milk in PBS (25 \u00b5L/well) for 1 hour at room temperature, then wash 4 times.\n4. Dilute our egg yolk IgY samples to 1.25 mg/mL in sample buffer and add 50 \u00b5L per well in triplicate. Include negative controls on each plate. Incubate for 1 hour at room temperature, then wash 4 times.\n5. Add 50 \u00b5L per well of anti-chicken IgY-HRP conjugate (Promega #G1351) diluted 1:30,000 in diluent. Incubate for 1 hour at room temperature, then wash 4 times.\n6. Add 50 \u00b5L per well of 1X TMB solution (Thermo Fisher #00-4201-56) and incubate for 15 minutes at room temperature in the dark.\n7. Stop the reaction by adding 50 \u00b5L of 3M HCl per well.\n8. Read absorbance on a plate reader at 450 nm.\n9. Calculate the positivity cut-off as 3 times the mean OD of the negative controls, and report back the raw OD values along with the final positive/negative determinations for all samples.", "thoughtSignature": ""}], "role": "model"}, "finishReason": "STOP", "index": 0}], "usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 756, "candidatesTokenCount": 397, "totalTokenCount": 2613, "promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT", "tokenCount": 756}], "thoughtsTokenCount": 1460, "serviceTier": "standard"}, "modelVersion": "gemini-3.6-flash", "responseId": "CBr3aoTWHOP1jrEPuczl0Ao"}